.TH "CHECKISOMD5" "1"
.SH "NAME"
checkisomd5 \(em check an MD5 checksum implanted by \fBimplantisomd5\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBcheckisomd5\fR [\fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP]  [\fB\-\-verbose\fP]  [\fB\-\-gauge\fP]  [\fB\-\-cert\fP \fIcertfile\fP]  [isofilename  | blockdevice ]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This manual page documents briefly the \fBcheckisomd5\fR command.  \fBcheckisomd5\fR is a program that checks an embedded MD5 checksum in an ISO9660 image (.iso), or block device.  The checksum is embedded by the corresponding \fBimplantisomd5\fR command.
.PP
With \fB\-\-cert\fP the detached signature \fIisofilename\fP.sig (created by \fBimplantisomd5 \-\-sign-key\fR) is verified against the public key in the certificate, and the result is reported as "Signature status: VALID" or "INVALID".  A VALID signature proves the embedded MD5 checksum was signed by the holder of the certificate's private key.
.PP
Verification requires three files provided together: the image itself, its detached signature \fIisofilename\fP.sig (in the same directory, with the same base name), and the certificate passed to \fB\-\-cert\fP.  If the \fI.sig\fP file is absent, the signature status is reported as "MISSING".  The private key is never needed for verification.
.PP
\fBcheckisomd5\fR trusts the public key contained in the supplied certificate; it does not check the certificate's trust chain, expiry or revocation.  Validate the certificate separately (for example with \fBopenssl verify\fR) if that is required.
.PP
The check can be aborted by pressing Esc key.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
Program returns exit status 0 if the checksum is correct, 1 if the checksum is incorrect or non-existent, or 2 if the check was aborted.  When \fB\-\-cert\fP is used, a failed signature verification also yields exit status 1.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-o\fP, \fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP" 10
Do not check the target.  Instead, output human-readable information about the target's checksums.  If a certificate serial number was embedded by \fBimplantisomd5 \-\-cert\fR, it is printed as well.
.IP "\fB\-\-cert\fP \fIcertfile\fP" 10
After the media check, verify the detached signature \fIisofilename\fP.sig against the public key in \fIcertfile\fP (PEM or DER).
.IP "\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-verbose\fP" 10
Display human-readable progress as the target is checked.  Without this option, nothing is outputted except errors.
.IP "\fB\-g\fP, \fB\-\-gauge\fP" 10
Display a series of numbers from 0 to 100, corresponding to check progress.  This output can be piped to \fBdialog \-\-gauge\fR for a user-friendly progress bar.
.IP "\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP" 10
Display a short usage message.
.SH "FILES"
.IP "\fIisofilename\fP.sig" 10
Detached base64 signature of the embedded MD5 checksum, produced by \fBimplantisomd5 \-\-sign-key\fR.  Must accompany the image for \fB\-\-cert\fP verification.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
implantisomd5 (1).
